diff --git a/TRIAGE.md b/TRIAGE.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..39da401
--- /dev/null
+++ b/TRIAGE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+# CI triage: build 1204 (test-isolated)
+
+- Root cause: the helper refactor put `total_weight_grams` and `round_to_minor` in `pricing.py`, so `shipping.py` and `tax.py` started importing `pricing`, while `pricing.py` imports `ShippingPolicy` and `TaxTable`/`compute_taxes` from them at module level: a shipping/tax <-> pricing import cycle.
+- It only breaks when shipping or tax is the first of the cycle to load: they run `from . import pricing`, pricing then asks the half-initialised shipping/tax module for a name it has not defined yet (ImportError: partially initialized module). Loaded pricing-first, the cycle happens to resolve.
+- Before #34 the eager `shopcore/__init__.py` always loaded pricing first; with lazy loading the first module touched decides. The full suite passes because `test_pricing.py` is collected before `test_shipping.py`/`test_tax.py`, but those modules fail on their own, as does any script importing `shopcore.tax` first.
+- Fix: moved the helpers to the lower-level modules they belong to (`order.total_weight_grams`, `money.round_to_minor`), so shipping and tax no longer import pricing and the module graph is acyclic; the lazy `__init__` is unchanged.
